# rpg/art/doll/clips/actions/spear.clip: PROPOSED by SLICE-ARMS (2026-10-23); SLICE-DOLL owns and commits it. The spear
# family on both bodies (STYLE_P2 25.8): the drawn guard (idle; walk and run below), the thrust (hit 1) and the block, in
# four facings. Timing at the hero's spear pace 1.1 (windup 77, strike 121, follow 143 ms): the loaded pose 77 ms; the
# impact 71 ms then the HIT-STOP beat (the same pose held 50 ms, the streak still at full length); the pull 70 ms; back
# on the guard 73 ms (0 px from the drawn idle). weapon=<deg>,front|back names the library angle (held/weapons/spear
# a<deg>); held= names the same view until the compositor picks angles itself. Facing up the spear is behind the body.
# (P2c slice iteration 1, INTEGRATE) SLICE-ARMS's proposed lines committed: the drawn idle / walk / run moved to `part drawn`,
# every clip gated `when spear` (a fighter's: a civil trade with the same tool keeps the generic clips).
# (INTEGRATE i2) SLICE-ARMS i2's lines (fD / fU foreshortened spear facing down / up, the lunge lean 4 on torso runl, the
# 60 ms settle before the guard); the drawn walk / run stay in spear_carry.clip (upright carry, B10; since fix round 2
# both fists on the haft: the guard facing D / U, the port facing R / L); the steps (at=) are
# tools/doll/p2c_weight.py's.
# (SLICE-ARMS i3 PROPOSAL) block: arms sp_brace (the haft raised across the body: R a067, L a112, D a045, U a135,back),
# legs buckle (the knees bent); the bob and steps kept; the old sp_block arms stay in the maps until this lands.

