# (P2c wave 2, ACTIONS-2H) the spear's other blows: hit 2 the higher thrust (the haft raised a step), hit 3 the lunge
# (a deeper coil, both arms at full reach, the step 5 px); the glaive's and the halberd's hit 3 the sweep (the haft
# over the back shoulder, down and forward at full reach, through), first so it wins for their forms; DEPTH: the guard
# set against a charge (crouched, the butt grounded, the head at a rider's chest) when the sim flags `spear-set`
# (FOLK-SIM-C's ask). Timing at pace 1.1 (finisher follow 308 ms). Written by ACTIONS-2H's tools/fams.py.
# (wave-2 fix round, ACTIONS r1, PLAN D81: no weapon pixel more than 2 rows below the sole row; both fists on the haft line
# in a drawn or action frame) hit 3 facing D thrusts the foreshortened spear (held=fD a337, as hits 1-2) on the thrust
# arms (sp_hit) with the lunge's lean, crouch and step: the straight-down a270 on sp_lunge ran the haft 20 rows under
# the soles (a stab into the ground), and no angle on sp_lunge holds the off fist on the haft above it. The glaive's and
# the halberd's sweep keep their diagonals with the strike's crouch a row shallower (bob 1: the head 3 rows under the
# soles at bob 2), and the follow facing D / U carries through on the strike's arms standing (sp_sws a337 / a202): the low
# sp_swf a315 / a225 ran the head 9-12 rows under the soles.
# (wave-2 fix round 2, ACTIONS; D81: the off fist on the haft line, 1.5 px, on every DRAWN and ACTION frame) facing D the
# guard's off arm is the thrust's (armL=sp_hit: the off fist a pixel up the foreshortened haft; the drawn idle, every
# blow's settle and the pull): sp_guard's left fist sat 1.5-1.7 px off the fD line (C3d: 220 lines); the spear itself does
# not move. Hit 3's settle stands back on the guard (at= gone, the sheath as hit 1's): it held the lunge's last pixel
# and snapped to the idle after it, and as its own atlas cut it put the T5 Jade glaive's ACTION at 516.5 KB of 512 (B10).
# (wave-2 fix round 3, ACTIONS; C3d) hit 3's lunge facing L holds the rear (far) fist back on the haft (sp_swf: the hands
# 9 px apart, not 6), so it reads behind the near arm instead of under its sleeve (44 lines, the heroine's e6w among them);
# the man's hit 1 pull facing L keeps the rear fist at the thrust's reach (sp_hit), the sleeve over sp_pull's (13 lines).
